AdaptiveCpp at ACPP_REF_WINDOWS: per-process OpenMP kernel libraries, non-throwing atomic_write (#108).

On Windows every process in a working directory shares one kernel cache
(current_path()/.acpp). The OpenMP backend wrote each kernel library to a path
derived only from the kernel configuration, loaded it from there and removed it
on destruction. A second process needing the same kernel renamed its copy onto a
library the first had loaded; Windows refused, atomic_write's throwing
fs::rename reached a noexcept frame on the worker thread, and the process
terminated (0xC0000409, FAST_FAIL_FATAL_APP_EXIT).

- omp_code_object.cpp: the library path carries the process id.
- filesystem.cpp: atomic_write uses the error_code overload of fs::rename and
  returns false on failure, removing its temporary file.

Applied by .github/actions/windows-toolchain before AdaptiveCpp is built. Still
present upstream on develop; drop this patch when ACPP_REF_WINDOWS includes a fix.

diff --git a/src/common/filesystem.cpp b/src/common/filesystem.cpp
index ed7dcd3..2cc3fdc 100644
--- a/src/common/filesystem.cpp
+++ b/src/common/filesystem.cpp
@@ -188,7 +188,16 @@ bool atomic_write(const std::string &filename, const std::string &data) {
   ostr.write(data.data(), data.size());
   ostr.close();
 
-  fs::rename(tmp_path, p);
+  // Non-throwing: callers report failure through the return value. On Windows the
+  // rename fails while another process has the target open or mapped, and a throw
+  // from here can reach a noexcept frame on a runtime worker thread.
+  std::error_code ec;
+  fs::rename(tmp_path, p, ec);
+  if(ec) {
+    std::error_code ignored;
+    fs::remove(tmp_path, ignored);
+    return false;
+  }
 
   return true;
 }
diff --git a/src/runtime/omp/omp_code_object.cpp b/src/runtime/omp/omp_code_object.cpp
index 5748d0d..dffe0e8 100644
--- a/src/runtime/omp/omp_code_object.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/omp/omp_code_object.cpp
@@ -14,6 +14,12 @@
 #include <sstream>
 #include <string>
 
+#ifdef _WIN32
+#include <process.h>
+#else
+#include <unistd.h>
+#endif
+
 #include "hipSYCL/runtime/backend.hpp"
 #include "hipSYCL/runtime/omp/omp_code_object.hpp"
 
@@ -31,6 +37,18 @@ namespace rt {
 
 namespace {
 
+// The kernel library is a per-process temporary file: it is loaded from this path and
+// removed when the executable object is destroyed. Processes sharing a kernel cache
+// directory must not share the path. On Windows a library that one process has loaded
+// can be neither replaced nor removed by another.
+std::string process_suffix() {
+#ifdef _WIN32
+  return std::to_string(_getpid());
+#else
+  return std::to_string(getpid());
+#endif
+}
+
 result make_shared_library_from_blob(void *&module, const std::string &blob,
                                      const std::string &cache_file) {
   // Write binary image to temporary file
@@ -67,7 +85,8 @@ omp_sscp_executable_object::omp_sscp_executable_object(
     const std::vector<std::string> &kernel_names,
     const kernel_configuration &config)
     : _hcf{hcf_source}, _id{config.generate_id()}, _module{nullptr},
-      _kernel_cache_path(kernel_cache::get_persistent_cache_file(_id) + "." + ACPP_SHARED_LIBRARY_EXTENSION) {
+      _kernel_cache_path(kernel_cache::get_persistent_cache_file(_id) + "." + process_suffix() + "." +
+                         ACPP_SHARED_LIBRARY_EXTENSION) {
   _build_result = build(binary, kernel_names);
